        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "How many creators do I need for a canvas UGC campaign?", a: "It depends on your target posting volume. A good starting point is 10-15 creators for a single account producing 30-40 videos per month. For multi-account programs, plan for 5-8 creators per account. OKAD handles creator recruitment from our network of 600+ vetted creators." },
          { q: "What industries work best for canvas UGC?", a: "Canvas UGC works across most consumer categories. The strongest results come from beauty, fitness, food/CPG, tech/SaaS, and fashion — industries where creator-style content feels natural. The model is less effective for B2B enterprise products with long sales cycles." },
          { q: "How long before I see results?", a: "Expect 1-3 weeks for account warmup, then 30-60 days to reach meaningful organic reach. Most well-run programs see consistent results by month 2-3. The key variable is posting volume — programs that post 30+ videos per month reach critical mass faster." },
          { q: "Can I use canvas UGC content for paid ads?", a: "Yes — this is one of the biggest advantages. Top organic performers become your paid ad creative through Spark Ads (TikTok) or Partnership Ads (Meta). Organic performance acts as a free testing signal, so you only spend ad budget on content that already proved it resonates." },
          { q: "What's the difference between canvas UGC and influencer marketing?", a: "In canvas UGC, creators post on brand-owned accounts and are paid per view. In influencer marketing, creators post on their own accounts and are paid per post or per campaign. Canvas UGC gives brands ownership of the audience and content library. See our full comparison at canvas UGC vs traditional UGC." },
          { q: "How much does a canvas UGC campaign cost?", a: "Creator payments typically run $2-$6 CPM. A program producing 100 videos per month generating 1M+ views costs roughly $3,000-$8,000/month in creator payments, plus agency management fees. Total program cost depends on account count, creator volume, and content complexity." },
        ].map((item) => (
